{"title":"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A movie theatre has eleven rows of seats. The rows are numbered from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Odd-numbered rows have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seats and even-numbered rows have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seats. How many seats are there in the theatre?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27ee01842dc34963dbfe26d32e85c46796ae1669.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 176 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 186 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 165 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 170 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 171$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"420\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are six odd-numbered rows (rows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/6809414c3449204ebeea5d4a2cab600244d1c29d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />).\nThese rows have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efe8d16e832ed21ee84f6252e80059d04cd713d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\times 15 = 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> seats in total.\nThere are five even-numbered rows (rows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/8688c979696b7120cb408d9b62f83a7ab222fe5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 4, 6, 8, 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" />).\nThese rows have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1bbfcfe669ed6d67938faa016c7e7b7623220a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\times 16 = 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> seats in total.\nTherefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/621c96cd9cda3835019227b87ac79a481122d65f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 + 80 = 170$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"14\" /> seats in total in the theatre.  The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-alig